# CHANGES.log

## 2026-08-28 — Scope lock, PRD.md created

Source: proposal review against requirements/Capstone_Requirements.pdf and docs/proposal.pdf.
All decisions below are reflected in PRD.md.

- D-001  Single-view metrology becomes the PRIMARY scale-recovery arm; the learned monocular
         depth model is demoted to baseline. Reason: monocular depth error at 2-3m is measured
         in inches against a 1/4" decision line; metrology on a near-planar scene with a
         known-size reference avoids absolute-depth estimation entirely.
         Supersedes: proposal Stage 2, which assumed a depth model under both arms.
- D-002  Dataset target cut from 100-150 entrances to 40-60, with more angles/distances per
         entrance. Reason: error-stratified-by-condition needs within-entrance variation;
         breadth leaves per-condition cells too small to interpret.
         Supersedes: proposal "Data and Ground Truth" target.
- D-003  Ground-truth instrument for threshold rise changed from tape measure (1/8") to digital
         caliper / depth gauge (+/-0.01"). Tape retained for clear width and ramp run. Reason:
         tape uncertainty was half the disputed quantity at the 1/4" line.
         Supersedes: proposal "Reference measurements: tape measure ... recorded to 1/8"".
- D-004  Stage 1 learned segmentation deferred to stretch; v1 uses human-tap ROI selection.
         Reason: fine-tuned segmentation requires a second hand-annotation job in the same five
         days as ground-truth capture, and detection is not the research question.
         Supersedes: proposal Stage 1.
- D-005  Demo is a native iOS app built as a THIN CLIENT: capture, upload, render; all metrology
         runs server-side in Python. Reason: keeps development in one language and protects
         Sep 6-8 for iteration rather than Core ML conversion. Introduces venue-connectivity
         dependency, tracked as R-4.
- D-006  Reference object for scale is a credit card (ISO/IEC 7810 ID-1, 85.60 x 53.98mm).
         Reason: spec-exact and already carried by ordinary users. Accepted cost: small in frame
         at realistic distance, tracked as R-3.
- D-007  Adopt written pre-registration plus a sealed test split (~30% of entrances, assigned at
         collection, unopened until results freeze 2026-09-07, run once). Reason: the stated
         contribution is an honest error budget; without this the negative-result framing does
         not survive scrutiny.
- D-008  Pre-registered primary success criterion: MAE <= 0.25" on threshold rise, with pass/fail
         classification against the ADA 1/2" line. The 1/4" line is reported as secondary.
         Reason: 1/2" is the consequential line (above it a ramp is required) and is honestly
         reachable.
- D-009  Abstention confirmed as a first-class output and a reported metric, not a failure mode.
- D-010  Team size confirmed at 4. Ownership in PRD.md section 9 assigned by role; names pending
         (open item O-1).
- D-011  PROPOSED, NOT LOCKED: split conformal prediction for confidence intervals, calibrated on
         a split distinct from the sealed test set. Must be settled before 2026-09-03 (open
         item O-4).

Scope explicitly unchanged from proposal: Track 2; threshold rise as the sole primary
measurement; glass doors treated as a documented failure class; no consumer map, no legal
compliance determinations.

Open items recorded in PRD.md section 12: team roster (O-1), caliper not yet purchased (O-2),
no tripod confirmed (O-3), D-011 unconfirmed (O-4), no ticket system despite CLAUDE.md section 5
requiring one (O-5).

## 2026-08-29 — Architecture review, ARCHITECTURE.md created

Source: design interview against PRD.md, docs/proposal.pdf and requirements/Capstone_Requirements.pdf.
All decisions below are reflected in PRD.md and ARCHITECTURE.md.

- D-012  Reference card is placed VERTICALLY against the riser face; Arm A recovers the rise
         in-plane from a homography on the card's four corners. Reason: scale and measurement
         share one surface, so the homography absorbs the projection — no intrinsics, no pose,
         no depth. Removes the largest unknown from the primary arm.
         Supersedes: PRD 5, Arm A stated as a ground-plane homography with a height offset,
         which cannot recover an out-of-plane height without intrinsics and pose.
- D-013  Three-arm usability gradient: A (vertical card) is the monocular accuracy ceiling,
         A-prime (card on ground) the realistic-user path, C (no card) the most usable. Reason:
         Arm A needs physical access to the step, which a wheelchair user at the bottom of it
         cannot do. D-006's "already in your pocket" rationale moves to Arm C, where it holds.
         Supersedes: D-001 framing of Arm A as the shipping path; D-006 rationale.
- D-014  Capture-only app built BEFORE dataset capture, on AVFoundation + CoreMotion. No ARKit.
         Reason: gives true intrinsics, gravity, LiDAR depth and full-resolution stills, and
         makes capture angle a measured quantity. ARKit's video frames are too small for an
         error budget counted in pixels across the rise.
         Supersedes: stock-camera dataset capture.
- D-015  Method boundary: one RGB still plus intrinsics and gravity. No depth map, no
         motion-derived scale. Reason: answers "why not just use ARKit?" — VIO recovers metric
         scale from motion, which would make the research question uninteresting. Enforced by
         construction, since no AR session is ever started.
- D-016  Metrology server on a cloud VM; demo fallback chain cellular -> venue wifi -> identical
         server image on a laptop -> pre-recorded. Reason: presentations are in an interior
         atrium, where cellular fails. Steps 1-3 run the same container image.
         Supersedes: R-4 mitigation "phone tether as primary backup".
- D-017  The seal is enforced in code: manifest with image hashes committed at capture, loader
         refuses sealed rows without an explicit flag, unsealing run appends to a committed
         audit log. Reason: "how do we know you didn't peek?" needs an answer that is not our
         word. Turns D-007 from a claim into an artefact.
- D-018  Dataset: bytes in object storage, records in git. Entrance ID and caliper reading are
         entered in the app at capture and written to a per-capture sidecar. Reason: low
         single-digit GB is the wrong shape for a repo; binding truth to image at the shutter
         press removes the reconciliation step where datasets rot.
- D-019  Capture angle pre-registered as a continuous error-versus-angle model on the sealed
         split; the other four condition variables reported from dev as exploratory. Reason:
         12-60 entrances with ~30% sealed give per-cell counts of one or two under a five-way
         stratification. A curve against a continuously measured angle is affordable; a
         contingency table is not. See Amendment A-1.
- D-020  LiDAR captured on EVERY entrance and quarantined from the metrology code path; loaded
         only by the evaluation harness. Reason: free once capture is instrumented, strengthens
         deliverable 5, and depth that sits where the method can reach it eventually gets used
         to tune.
         Supersedes: PRD 6, LiDAR on a matched subset.

AMENDMENT to the pre-registration (PRD 2), logged per that section's own rule:

- A-1    Stratification analysis plan. The five stratification variables are unchanged. What
         changed is which of them the sealed run tests confirmatorily: capture angle becomes a
         continuous error-versus-angle model on the sealed split, and the remaining four move to
         the dev split as exploratory. Reason: statistical power at the sealed sample size, as
         set out in D-019. Capture angle became continuously measurable only when capture moved
         into an instrumented app (D-014). Committed 2026-08-29, before first capture and before
         any image was processed. To be reported as an amendment at Demo Day.

New risks, recorded in ARCHITECTURE.md section 11:

- R-7    App signing is on the critical path for the whole dataset, not just the demo;
         free-account builds expire after 7 days, landing mid-capture.
- R-8    Fewer capture devices than the parallel field tracks in PRD 9 assume. Unknown until the
         roster is assigned (O-1). Response is to cut the entrance target, not the protocol.
- R-9    Calibration-data delivery may not be available on the team's actual devices. Verified
         day one; ARKit is the fallback, at the resolution cost in ARCHITECTURE.md section 2.
- R-10   LiDAR is commonly reported at around +/-1cm, coarser than the 0.25" bar and comparable
         to the 1/2" line itself, so the "accuracy ceiling" may sit below the success criterion.
         Bench-test in week one; if confirmed, deliverable 5 is reframed.
- R-11   Demo app and capture app drift apart, so Demo Day exhibits uncharacterised behaviour.
         Mitigated structurally: the demo app is the capture app plus rendering.

Repo hygiene: CHANGES.log was matched by the boilerplate `*.log` rule in .gitignore and was
therefore untracked — the decision log underpinning D-007 had no version history. Added a
negation rule so it is versioned from this commit forward.

Ticket tracker chosen: GitHub Issues on this repo (O-5). Backlog not yet filed.

Scope explicitly unchanged: Track 2; threshold rise as the sole primary measurement; the
pre-registered primary metric, success criterion and decision lines in PRD 2; glass doors as a
documented failure class; no consumer map, no legal compliance determinations.

## 2026-08-30 — Split seed committed (TICK-011, issue #19)

Source: GitHub issue #19, making D-007's sealed split a checkable assignment rather than a
promise. Committed before the first capture.

- Split seed committed in src/frontdoor/split_seed.json at commit
  bab15548d9439ea3ff6aa0579cb4a35ceb5f199d (2026-08-30). Assignment is
  sha256(entrance_id + seed), first 8 bytes as a big-endian unsigned integer mod 100: below 30
  sealed, below 50 calib, otherwise dev. Documented in src/frontdoor/split.py and reproducible
  by a third party from the seed file and that description alone; `python -m frontdoor.split`
  prints the assignment for any list of entrance IDs.
- Target proportions fixed at 30% sealed / 20% calib / 50% dev. The PRD fixes only the ~30%
  sealed share (D-007). The 20% calib share exists so that split conformal prediction (D-011,
  unconfirmed, O-4) has a held-out set distinct from sealed without carving one out after
  capture. If D-011 is dropped, calib folds back into dev at analysis time; no assignment is
  ever changed.
- Over 1000 synthetic IDs the seed yields 30.3% sealed / 18.4% calib / 51.3% dev. The actual
  proportions over the real entrance IDs are to be recorded here once capture completes.

## 2026-08-31 — Roster reality, free-tier infrastructure

Source: TEAM.md device audit (TICK-003, #15) and a cost decision taken by the team.

- D-025  Paid Apple Developer Program will NOT be purchased. The capture app is signed with FREE
         PROVISIONING and installed over a cable from a team Mac. Reason: the app needs no
         paid-gated capability -- AVFoundation capture, depth delivery and CoreMotion require only
         Info.plist usage descriptions. Accepted cost: builds expire after 7 days (R-7), so signing
         becomes a scheduled activity rather than a one-off. A build signed 2026-08-31 expires
         2026-09-07, BEFORE Demo Day, so a re-sign no later than 2026-09-06 is mandatory.
         Compounding factor: James holds the only LiDAR device and runs Windows, so he cannot
         re-sign his own build; every install for him is a physical session with a Mac owner.
         Supersedes: TICK-001's requirement to enrol and pay by 2026-08-29.
- D-026  All hosted infrastructure runs on PROVIDER FREE TIERS. No spend is authorised for object
         storage or the server host. Reason: cost decision. Consequences that are now load-bearing:
         projected dataset volume is 2-5 GB, so a 5 GB allowance is marginal and 10 GB comfortable;
         billing must be incapable of starting silently; and the D-020 depth quarantine must be
         satisfied by TWO BUCKETS where a provider scopes credentials per bucket rather than per
         prefix -- the denial is the requirement, not the layout.
         Open, and required before TICK-062 (#50) closes: which arms POST /measure serves live (a
         free instance may not hold the depth model), and whether the evaluation harness runs on
         the free host or locally on a team Mac. The latter contradicts the "bucket beside the VM"
         premise in ARCHITECTURE sections 7-8 and must be logged if chosen.
         Supersedes: the unstated assumption in D-016 and D-018 that hosting would be paid.
- A-1/A-3  FALSIFIED by the device audit; recorded in ARCHITECTURE section 10 and TEAM.md section 2.
         R-8 has fired. Its response rule does not clear the binding constraint: D-020 requires
         LiDAR on every entrance and only one device produces it. Relaxing D-020 to a matched
         subset remains an OPEN protocol decision, deliberately not taken here.

- D-027  Tickets are ASSIGNED, not self-assigned. Every open issue names an owner in GitHub,
         following the work division in TEAM.md section 3. Reason: the self-assign-and-rotate
         convention left the whole backlog owner-less, and the device audit showed the division is
         constrained by hardware rather than preference -- only one person can capture entrances,
         and only one can build and test the capture app unaided. An unowned backlog cannot express
         that. Work may still move between people; the rule is to REASSIGN rather than clear, so no
         ticket is ever left without a name against it.
         Supersedes: D-010's "ownership assigned by role, names pending", O-1's self-assign
         convention, and the "Unassigned by design" footer previously carried by 90 tickets.

## 2026-08-31 — Canonical entrance ID form (TICK-217, issue #105)

Source: GitHub issue #105. Settled before first capture so a mistyped ID cannot silently
land an entrance in a different split (D-007, D-017).

- Form: ASCII `E-` followed by exactly three digits (`E-014`). Character set is ASCII
  as constrained by that pattern; length is 5 characters.
- Case: the prefix is uppercase `E`. Lowercase `e-014` is canonicalised to `E-014`.
- Surrounding whitespace (spaces, tabs, CR, LF) is stripped. Internal whitespace is rejected.
- Unicode: NFC normalisation is applied before the pattern check. NFD/NFC pairs of the same
  string therefore agree; IDs that are not `E-NNN` after NFC+strip+upper are rejected, not
  coerced (accented letters, fullwidth letters, extra digits).
- Canonicalise case and surrounding whitespace, because those are the operator errors that
  would otherwise split one entrance in two. Reject everything else, so a sidecar cannot
  store an ID the split tool would refuse.
- Enforced in `frontdoor.split.canonical_entrance_id`, used by `assign_split` and the CLI,
  and by the sidecar schema `entrance_id` pattern. The capture app (TICK-024, #28) must
  create IDs in this form; it does not yet specify one.

## Decision-log gap — D-021 to D-024 and Amendment A-2 reconstructed, NOT original text

These four decision IDs are referenced throughout the ticket backlog but were never written into
this log. The statements below are RECONSTRUCTED from how each ID is used in tickets, and need
confirmation by whoever took the original decisions. They are recorded so the IDs resolve to
something rather than dangling; they are not claimed to be the original wording.

- D-021  (reconstructed) Per-entrance shot plan is enforced by the instrument: the app tells the
         operator which card placement, angle bucket and distance bucket remain outstanding and
         refuses to mark the entrance complete until the plan is met. Arm A-prime ground-card
         frames are requested only for entrances in the A-prime subset, whose membership is fixed
         in advance by a documented rule. Referenced by: #31, #72, #85, #91.
- D-022  (reconstructed) Compliance verdicts are reported for Arm A ONLY. No pass/fail bar or
         threshold line is attached to Arms A-prime, B or C; those arms report measurement error
         alone. Referenced by: #91, #93, #95, #72.
- D-023  (reconstructed) Three-way split -- dev, calib, sealed -- assigned deterministically from a
         committed seed at entrance creation and immutable thereafter, with calib reserved for
         interval calibration so conformal intervals are never calibrated on dev or on sealed data.
         Referenced by: #45, #53, #84.
- D-024  (reconstructed) One capture writes one image, one depth map and one JSON sidecar, hashed
         at the shutter press, with entrance ID, caliper ground truth and condition tags bound in
         at capture time rather than reconciled afterwards. Referenced by: #32, #83, #85.

- A-2    (reconstructed) AMENDMENT TO THE PRE-REGISTRATION. The pre-registered success criterion
         -- MAE <= 0.25" on threshold rise, on the sealed test split (PRD section 2, D-008) -- is
         judged against ARM A ONLY. Arms A-prime, B and C are reported without any pass/fail bar.
         Reason, as stated in the tickets that cite it: leaving the arm unnamed would let the
         hypothesis be scored against whichever arm looked best once results were seen, which is
         the exact failure D-007 exists to prevent. Referenced by: #7, #10, #37, #56, #63, #71,
         #73, #90, #93.
         RECONSTRUCTED FROM TICKET USAGE, and more urgently in need of confirmation than the four
         above: PRD section 2 states that nothing in it changes after 2026-08-28 and that
         amendments are logged here with a reason AND REPORTED AS SUCH AT DEMO DAY. Recorded here
         so the amendment is not silently absent from the log, but the DATE it was taken and its
         original wording are not recoverable from the tickets and must be supplied by whoever
         took the decision. Until then this entry establishes that A-2 exists and what it does,
         not when it was agreed. See TICK-231.
